    "97f512db92": {
      "id": "97f512db92",
      "created": 1795011010.187308,
      "headline": "GTA 6 Car Alarms: How to Steal Cars Without Alerting Cops",
      "url": "https://www.videogameschronicle.com/guide/gta-6-car-alarms-explained-how-to-steal-cars-with-alarms-in-gta-6/",
      "source": "VGC",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011005/gta-bot/97f512db92-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011005/gta-bot/97f512db92-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011006/gta-bot/97f512db92-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011007/gta-bot/97f512db92-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011008/gta-bot/97f512db92-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795011009/gta-bot/97f512db92-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Car theft in Leonida isn't as simple as it used to be. 🚗\n\nMany cars are alarmed, and breaking into one early on can alert the police and nearby pedestrians. The answer is the Slim Jim, a tool that gets you into standard cars quietly. Swipe for how it works and what to do before you have it.\n\nHow are you handling alarmed cars so far?\n\nSource: VideoGamesChronicle\n\n#GTA6 #GrandTheftAutoVI #GTAVI #Leonida #RockstarGames #GTA6Tips #GTA6Guide #GamingTips #VideoGames #GTA",
      "alt_text": "Graphic with the headline about how to steal alarmed cars in GTA 6 without alerting the police, labelled Tips & Tricks.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "TIPS & TRICKS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Alarms are everywhere",
          "text": "Many of the cars you can steal in Leonida are alarmed. Breaking into one early in the game alerts the police and the pedestrians around you."
        },
        {
          "title": "The Slim Jim fix",
          "text": "A Slim Jim lets you get into standard cars without smashing the window or carjacking anyone. That means you can steal them without alerting the police."
        },
        {
          "title": "Not for supercars",
          "text": "The Slim Jim only works on standard cars. Supercars and Hypercars need a later-game tool, and key cloning comes much further into the story."
        },
        {
          "title": "Before you get it",
          "text": "You get the Slim Jim in chapter two, around 10 hours in. Until then, try late at night when traffic is light and grab a car heading for the highway. Cops are less likely to chase you there."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1794996706/Boobie_Ike_01.jpg",
      "text_message_id": 39
    },
    "c2dd93809f": {
      "id": "c2dd93809f",
      "created": 1795014625.1741796,
      "headline": "No Mission Replays in GTA 6, So Use Your Save Slots",
      "url": "https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-multiple-save-files-replay-missions",
      "source": "Eurogamer",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014589/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014589/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014590/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014590/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014591/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795014592/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Plan your saves, Leonida. 💾 GTA 6 has no mission replay option, so once you finish a story mission you can't jump back into it. The game gives you 15 save slots plus an auto-save as a safety net. Rockstar also says it designed missions to be harder to fail, so you can experiment and play your own way. Swipe for the details.\n\nWill you keep a save before every big story moment, or trust the auto-save?\n\nSource: Eurogamer\n\n#GTA6 #GTAVI #GrandTheftAutoVI #Rockstar #RockstarGames #Leonida #GTA #GTA6Tips #PS5 #XboxSeriesX",
      "alt_text": "News graphic explaining that GTA 6 has no mission replay feature and offers 15 save slots instead.",
      "score": 8,
      "reel_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/video/upload/v1795014624/gta-bot/c2dd93809f-reel.mp4",
      "category": "NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "No mission replays",
          "text": "Once you finish a story mission in GTA 6, you can't replay it. Eurogamer's reviewer confirmed this over a 100+ hour playthrough. GTA 5 did offer a Replay Mission option."
        },
        {
          "title": "15 save slots instead",
          "text": "You get 15 save slots plus an auto-save for when you get Busted or Wasted. Missions far outnumber slots, so save wisely. Eurogamer says big story missions are easy to spot."
        },
        {
          "title": "Harder to fail",
          "text": "Rockstar's David Hynd says the team wanted fewer mission fails for players trying something different. Missions were built with many ways to approach them."
        },
        {
          "title": "Freedom over simplicity",
          "text": "Hynd admits that keeping missions open is harder in such a big game, but says the freedom was worth it. Players are expected to learn the world's rules and reapply them."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1794996750/Jason_and_Lucia_04.jpg",
      "text_message_id": 47
    }
  },
